# ONE health feature, NOT a Rift lifecycle/combat test. Run only after the
# coordinator applies the HP-only SQL and grants the entry-specific cache reload.
# Fresh map-35 instance; only temporary copies of the four Fire roles and
# three support references. No persistent NPC spawn, actual Rift or config edit.
# Expected HP assumes level 80 and the observed normal/elite HP rates of 1.
name    Rifts - Fire support matches peer health without changing other Fire roles
timeout 60s
bot w warrior
place 35 -46.262 177.5 -40.0506 4.72486
do gm target gm
require gm alive
require gm map 35
as gm .reload creature_template 80017

# Create all fixtures before checking them. No attack/loot/equip action.
as gm .npc add temp 80039
pick fire_melee creature:80039
as gm .npc add temp 80041
pick fire_caster creature:80041
as gm .npc add temp 80047
pick fire_disruptor creature:80047
as gm .npc add temp 80017
pick fire_support creature:80017
as gm .npc add temp 80035
pick shadow_support creature:80035
as gm .npc add temp 80046
pick air_support creature:80046
as gm .npc add temp 80175
pick water_support creature:80175
wait 1s

expect fire_melee alive
expect fire_melee maxhealth == 90814
expect fire_caster alive
expect fire_caster maxhealth == 63563
expect fire_disruptor alive
expect fire_disruptor maxhealth == 93475
expect fire_support alive
expect fire_support maxhealth == 72658
expect fire_support maxhealth == maxhealth:shadow_support
expect fire_support maxhealth == maxhealth:air_support
expect fire_support maxhealth == maxhealth:water_support
expect fire_support health == 100%
log measured fresh template health; no claim about damage combat or a complete Rift wave

cleanup
# Every selected alias is a picked test-only temporary copy. .die removes
# TEMPSUMMON_CORPSE_DESPAWN copies on their next update. If an add/pick failed,
# cleanup records an error; it must never substitute an entry search or kill
# nearby world creatures. The initial selection is the test director; later
# selections are only owned fixtures. A missing alias cannot redirect a kill
# to a world spawn. On fixture failure even cleanup is reported FAILED.
do gm target fire_melee
as gm .die
do gm target fire_caster
as gm .die
do gm target fire_disruptor
as gm .die
do gm target fire_support
as gm .die
do gm target shadow_support
as gm .die
do gm target air_support
as gm .die
do gm target water_support
as gm .die
waitfor fire_melee missing timeout 3s
waitfor fire_caster missing timeout 3s
waitfor fire_disruptor missing timeout 3s
waitfor fire_support missing timeout 3s
waitfor shadow_support missing timeout 3s
waitfor air_support missing timeout 3s
waitfor water_support missing timeout 3s
log rift_fire_support_health done
